## Model card (verified facts, no scores)

- **Name:** Nemotron 3.5 Bolt E4B (4GB) — "E4B" = the 4GB-memory edge member of NVIDIA's Bolt tier.
- **Short description:** NVIDIA's announced open edge model "optimized for intelligence per GB for fast conversational agents" — built for physical/conversational agents (fast local voice assistants, interactive characters, embedded interfaces) on GeForce RTX, Jetson, and RTX/DGX Spark. Part of the Nemotron 3.5 family (Lightning = high throughput, Ultra = hardest reasoning, Super VL = 120B multimodal, Bolt = edge). Not an alias.
- **Provider / access:** **None verified.** AI Agent Store (checked 2026-10-16): "could not confirm a model ID for general API access"; no hosted rate verified; targeted local-device release. Expect HuggingFace `nvidia/*` + Ollama/llama.cpp like its sibling on release day; not present yet (2026-10-16 searches surfaced no E4B checkpoint — only `nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Bolt-74B-A9B-24GB` variants). Repo `meta.json`'s scaffolded `opencode/nemotron-3.5-bolt-e4b` ID is unconfirmed (meta left untouched, flagged for orchestrator).
- **Release / knowledge:** Announced 2026-10-15 (NVIDIA blog, https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/nemotron-3-5-super-vl/); **scheduled release 2026-10-23** (NVIDIA official "Super VL and Bolt 74B-A9B are available now, with Bolt E4B coming Oct. 23"; corroborated by aiagentstore.ai "announced for October 23"). Knowledge cutoff not posted.
- **Conflict resolved:** ai-trend.me's headline claims E4B was "officially released" Oct 15 alongside the 74B — first-party NVIDIA wording wins: only the 74B-A9B 24GB shipped Oct 15; E4B ships Oct 23. (ai-trend's own Ollama paragraph describes Super VL support, not E4B.)
- **IDs:** none downloadable/verified as of 2026-10-16.
- **Context window:** no verified public figure (scaffold placeholder said 128K — unconfirmed; do not rely).
- **Modalities:** conversational + multi-turn agentic text presumably (NVIDIA: "combines natural conversation with multi-turn agentic capabilities"); voice-assistant/embedded positioning implies speech I/O via pipelines, but no modality list is published. Unverified.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-16):** unverified — AI Agent Store lists input/output/cache as "Provider specifications · prices unverified"; family is open-weights (sibling Bolt 74B is OpenMDW-1.1, but E4B's license is unpublished).
- **Architecture:** unpublished for E4B — 4GB memory footprint is the only hard spec (NVIDIA blog + ai-trend). Sibling facts NOT transferable: Bolt 74B-A9B is 74B/9B MoE, native 2-bit QAT, 256K context, OpenMDW-1.1 (S5 Labs, model card).

